WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.499
Sense occurs again after
Land and an adoption period.

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:08.731
The second reading asks whether the Frame Card
outcome appears in the operator’s workflow.

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:14.177
Distinguish available software, attempted
use, reviewed decisions, and sustained use.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:19.218
Count eligible work rather than all work
if the tool serves only one category.

00:00:19.288 --> 00:00:22.595
Examine overrides and
abandonment alongside speed.

00:00:22.665 --> 00:00:28.467
The original prediction remains the comparison
point unless a documented change occurred

00:00:28.537 --> 00:00:29.881
before the new test.

00:00:29.951 --> 00:00:34.325
Two weeks later, forty of one hundred
eligible tickets use assistance.

00:00:34.395 --> 00:00:40.496
Completed assisted reviews remain faster, but
adoption is below the pre-agreed 70 percent

00:00:40.566 --> 00:00:42.102
exercise threshold.

00:00:42.172 --> 00:00:45.991
The tool is available without
achieving the full adoption target.

00:00:46.061 --> 00:00:50.839
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

00:00:50.909 --> 00:00:54.771
Write the second delta entry and
recommend the next gate decision.

00:00:54.841 --> 00:01:00.131
Observed adoption is forty percent, using
eligible tickets as the denominator.

00:01:00.201 --> 00:01:04.148
Investigate friction and incentives
with agents before scaling.

00:01:04.218 --> 00:01:07.610
Iterate on workflow fit while
preserving quality checks.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:13.504
Do not erase the seventy percent threshold or
report only the successful assisted subset.

00:01:13.574 --> 00:01:18.182
The second reading prevents a technically
successful slice from becoming an unsupported

00:01:18.252 --> 00:01:19.489
outcome claim.

00:01:19.559 --> 00:01:21.863
What does the second Sense reading evaluate?

00:01:21.933 --> 00:01:24.365
A. Only whether the code compiles B.

00:01:24.435 --> 00:01:26.483
Only prototype accuracy C.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.836
Outcome and adoption after landing.

00:01:28.906 --> 00:01:30.314
The best answer is C.

00:01:30.384 --> 00:01:33.925
The second reading checks the
operating consequence over time.
